<title>UK: Licht cuts estimate of world 96/97 molasses output.</title>
<headline>Licht cuts estimate of world 96/97 molasses output.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>World molasses production should reach 43.5 million tonnes in 1996/97, down from the previous estimate of 45.0 million, German statistician F.O. Licht said on Thursday.</p>
<p>World output reached 45.1 million tonnes in 1995/96, Licht said.</p>
<p>Licht said it was primarily molasses production in Asia which had been significantly scaled down after the extent of crop failures in India, Thailand and Indonesia became apparent.</p>
<p>Indian cane molasses production was forecast to fall to 6.0 million tonnes this season, down from 7.25 million the previous year.</p>
<p>Molasses production in Thailand -- one of the major forces on the world market -- finished at 2.6 million tonnes, down from 2.83 million in 1995/96, Licht said.</p>
<p>Total 1996/97 output in Indonesia reached no more than 1.16 million tonnes after 1.32 the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Jeremy Smith, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8064</p>
